        <link>https://www.theblock.co/learn/ecosystems/what-is-zcash-zec-435779</link>
        <media:content url="https://www.tbstat.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1600,height=900,fit=cover,format=jpeg,quality=80/wp/uploads/2026/11/zcash-glyph-16x9-1.png" type="image/*" medium="image"/>        <guid isPermaLink="false">391e961a-f6c3-59bd-8293-88faa1772ae8</guid>
        <pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 02:36:01 +0000</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[Zcash (ZEC) is a privacy coin and blockchain launched in 2016. It allows users to make both public and private transactions. The latter — called “shielded transactions” on the network — make use of zero-knowledge proofs called zk-SNARKs to verify payments without revealing the sender, recipient or amount. Zcash has emerged as one of the […]]]></description>            <dc:creator><![CDATA[The Block Research]]></dc:creator>
